{"surah": 82, "verses": [{"ayah": 1, "text": "إِذَا ٱلسَّمَآءُ ٱنفَطَرَتْ ", "translation": "When the sky breaks apart", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلسَّمَآءُ", "translit": "ُءٓāَmَّslٱ", "root": "سمو"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱنفَطَرَتْ", "translit": "ْtَrَṭَfnٱ", "root": "فطر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 2, "text": "وَإِذَا ٱلْكَوَاكِبُ ٱنتَثَرَتْ ", "translation": "And when the stars fall, scattering,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْكَوَاكِبُ", "translit": "ُbِkāَwَkْlٱ", "root": "كوكب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱنتَثَرَتْ", "translit": "ْtَrَhtَtnٱ", "root": "نثر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 3, "text": "وَإِذَا ٱلْبِحَارُ فُجِّرَتْ ", "translation": "And when the seas are erupted", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْبِحَارُ", "translit": "ُrāَḥِbْlٱ", "root": "بحر"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فُجِّرَتْ", "translit": "ْtَrِّjgُf", "root": "فجر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 4, "text": "وَإِذَا ٱلْقُبُورُ بُعْثِرَتْ ", "translation": "And when the [contents of] graves are scattered [i.e., exposed],", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْقُبُورُ", "translit": "ُrwُbُqْlٱ", "root": "قبر"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بُعْثِرَتْ", "translit": "ْtَrِhtْʿعُb", "root": "بعثر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 5, "text": "عَلِمَتْ نَفْسٌ مَّا قَدَّمَتْ وَأَخَّرَتْ ", "translation": "A soul will [then] know what it has put forth and kept back.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "عَلِمَتْ", "translit": "ْtَmِlَʿع", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "نَفْسٌ", "translit": "ٌsْfَn", "root": "نفس"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَّا", "translit": "āَّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "قَدَّمَتْ", "translit": "ْtَmَّdَq", "root": "قدم"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَأَخَّرَتْ", "translit": "ْtَrَّhkَaʾَw", "root": "اخر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 6, "text": "يَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلْإِنسَٰنُ مَا غَرَّكَ بِرَبِّكَ ٱلْكَرِيمِ ", "translation": "O mankind, what has deceived you concerning your Lord, the Generous,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "يَٰٓأَيُّهَا", "translit": "āَhُّyَaʾَٰٓy", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْإِنسَٰنُ", "translit": "ُnَٰsnِiʾْlٱ", "root": "انس"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "غَرَّكَ", "translit": "َkَّrَغ", "root": "غرر"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "بِرَبِّكَ", "translit": "َkِّbَrِb", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلْكَرِيمِ", "translit": "ِmyِrَkْlٱ", "root": "كرم"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 7, "text": "ٱلَّذِى خَلَقَكَ فَسَوَّىٰكَ فَعَدَلَكَ ", "translation": "Who created you, proportioned you, and balanced you?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِى", "translit": "àِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "خَلَقَكَ", "translit": "َkَqَlَhk", "root": "خلق"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فَسَوَّىٰكَ", "translit": "َkٰàَّwَsَf", "root": "سوي"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فَعَدَلَكَ", "translit": "َkَlَdَʿعَf", "root": "عدل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 8, "text": "فِىٓ أَىِّ صُورَةٍ مَّا شَآءَ رَكَّبَكَ ", "translation": "In whatever form He willed has He assembled you.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَىِّ", "translit": "ِّàَaʾ", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "صُورَةٍ", "translit": "ٍẗَrwُṣ", "root": "صور"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مَّا", "translit": "āَّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "شَآءَ", "translit": "َءٓāَhs", "root": "شيا"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "رَكَّبَكَ", "translit": "َkَbَّkَr", "root": "ركب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 9, "text": "كَلَّا بَلْ تُكَذِّبُونَ بِٱلدِّينِ ", "translation": "No! But you deny the Recompense.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "كَلَّا", "translit": "āَّlَk", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بَلْ", "translit": "ْlَb", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "تُكَذِّبُونَ", "translit": "َnwُbِّhdَkُt", "root": "كذب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "بِٱلدِّينِ", "translit": "ِnyِّdlٱِb", "root": "دين"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 10, "text": "وَإِنَّ عَلَيْكُمْ لَحَٰفِظِينَ ", "translation": "And indeed, [appointed] over you are keepers,[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَلَيْكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَحَٰفِظِينَ", "translit": "َnyِẓِfَٰḥَl", "root": "حفظ"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 11, "text": "كِرَامًا كَٰتِبِينَ ", "translation": "Noble and recording;", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "كِرَامًا", "translit": "āًmāَrِk", "root": "كرم"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "كَٰتِبِينَ", "translit": "َnyِbِtَٰk", "root": "كتب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 12, "text": "يَعْلَمُونَ مَا تَفْعَلُونَ ", "translation": "They know whatever you do.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "يَعْلَمُونَ", "translit": "َnwُmَlْʿعَy", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "تَفْعَلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlَʿعْfَt", "root": "فعل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 13, "text": "إِنَّ ٱلْأَبْرَارَ لَفِى نَعِيمٍ ", "translation": "Indeed, the righteous will be in pleasure,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْأَبْرَارَ", "translit": "َrāَrْbَaʾْlٱ", "root": "برر"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَفِى", "translit": "àِfَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "نَعِيمٍ", "translit": "ٍmyِʿعَn", "root": "نعم"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 14, "text": "وَإِنَّ ٱلْفُجَّارَ لَفِى جَحِيمٍ ", "translation": "And indeed, the wicked will be in Hellfire.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْفُجَّارَ", "translit": "َrāَّjgُfْlٱ", "root": "فجر"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَفِى", "translit": "àِfَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "جَحِيمٍ", "translit": "ٍmyِḥَjg", "root": "جحم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 15, "text": "يَصْلَوْنَهَا يَوْمَ ٱلدِّينِ ", "translation": "They will [enter to] burn therein on the Day of Recompense,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "يَصْلَوْنَهَا", "translit": "āَhَnْwَlْṣَy", "root": "صلي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَوْمَ", "translit": "َmْwَy", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلدِّينِ", "translit": "ِnyِّdlٱ", "root": "دين"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 16, "text": "وَمَا هُمْ عَنْهَا بِغَآئِبِينَ ", "translation": "And never therefrom will they be absent.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "هُمْ", "translit": "ْmُh", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَنْهَا", "translit": "āَhْnَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "بِغَآئِبِينَ", "translit": "َnyِbِyʾٓāَغِb", "root": "غيب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 17, "text": "وَمَآ أَدْرَىٰكَ مَا يَوْمُ ٱلدِّينِ ", "translation": "And what can make you know what is the Day of Recompense?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَدْرَىٰكَ", "translit": "َkٰàَrْdَaʾ", "root": "دري"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يَوْمُ", "translit": "ُmْwَy", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلدِّينِ", "translit": "ِnyِّdlٱ", "root": "دين"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 18, "text": "ثُمَّ مَآ أَدْرَىٰكَ مَا يَوْمُ ٱلدِّينِ ", "translation": "Then, what can make you know what is the Day of Recompense?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ثُمَّ", "translit": "َّmُht", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مَآ", "translit": "ٓāَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَدْرَىٰكَ", "translit": "َkٰàَrْdَaʾ", "root": "دري"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "يَوْمُ", "translit": "ُmْwَy", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلدِّينِ", "translit": "ِnyِّdlٱ", "root": "دين"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 19, "text": "يَوْمَ لَا تَمْلِكُ نَفْسٌ لِّنَفْسٍ شَيْـًٔاۖ وَٱلْأَمْرُ يَوْمَئِذٍ لِّلَّهِ ", "translation": "It is the Day when a soul will not possess for another soul [power to do] a thing; and the command, that Day, is [entirely] with Allāh.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "يَوْمَ", "translit": "َmْwَy", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "تَمْلِكُ", "translit": "ُkِlْmَt", "root": "ملك"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "نَفْسٌ", "translit": "ٌsْfَn", "root": "نفس"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "لِّنَفْسٍ", "translit": "ٍsْfَnِّl", "root": "نفس"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "شَيْـًٔا", "translit": "āًٔـْyَhs", "root": "شيا"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَٱلْأَمْرُ", "translit": "ُrْmَaʾْlٱَw", "root": "امر"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "يَوْمَئِذٍ", "translit": "ٍhdِyʾَmْwَy", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "لِّلَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّlِّl", "root": "اله"}], "hasIhya": true}], "tafsir": {"6": [{"arabic": "يوم يساق العباد ومعهم الأشهاد ويشيب الصغير ويسكر الكبير فيومئذ وضعت الموازين ونشرت الدواوين وبرزت الجحيم وأغلى الحميم وزفرت النار ويئس الكفار وسعرت النيران وتغيرت الألوان وخرس اللسان ونطقت جوارح الإنسان فيا أيها الإنسان ما غرك بربك الكريم حيث أغلقت الأبواب وأرخيت الستور واستترت عن الخلائق فقارفت الفجور فماذا تفعل وقد شهدت عليك جوارحك فالويل كل الويل لنا معشر الغافلين", "english": "The day when the servants (of Allah) are driven forth, and with them are the witnesses, and the young turn gray-haired and the old become intoxicated. Then on that day, the scales are set up, the records are spread open, Hellfire is made manifest, the boiling water is heated, the Fire blazes forth, the disbelievers despair, the fires are kindled, the colors change, the tongue falls silent, and the limbs of the human being speak. 'O human being! What has deluded you concerning your Generous Lord (Rabbika al-Karim)?' For the doors have been closed, the curtains have been lowered, and you have concealed yourself from the creatures, yet you committed immorality. So what will you do when your limbs bear witness against you? Then woe upon woe to us, the heedless ones.", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book10.doc.txt", "book_title": "Book of Repentance", "content_type": "ethics", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the diseases of the heart and their cure, from 'Book of Repentance'", "badge": "Ethics"}], "10": [{"arabic": "قال عطاء بن أبي رباح: إن من كان قبلكم كانوا يكرهون فضول الكلام وكانوا يعدون فضول الكلام ما عدا كتاب الله تعالى وسنة رسول الله ﭬ، أو أمراً بمعروف أو نهياً عن منكر، أو أن تنطق بحاجتك في معيشتك التي لا بد لك منها، أتنكرون أن عليكم حافظين كراماً كاتبين عن اليمين وعن الشمال قعيد ما يلفظ من قول إلا لديه رقيب عتيد، أما يستحي أحدكم إذا نشرت صحيفته التي أملاها صدر نهاره كان أكثر ما فيها ليس من أمر دينه ولا دنياه.", "english": "Ata ibn Abi Rabah said: Those who came before you used to hate superfluous speech, and they considered superfluous speech to be anything except the Book of Allah the Exalted and the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), or commanding good or forbidding evil, or speaking of your need in your livelihood which is indispensable for you. Do you deny that upon you are noble guardians (Hafizin) writing from the right and from the left seated? Not a word is uttered except that with him is a ready observer. Does not one of you feel ashamed when his record is spread out which he dictated at the beginning of his day, and most of what is in it is not from the matter of his religion nor his worldly life?", "book_file": "vol3_Vol3-book4a.doc.txt", "book_title": "Condemnation of Anger and Hatred", "content_type": "ethics", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the diseases of the heart and their cure, from 'Condemnation of Anger and Hatred'", "badge": "Ethics"}], "13": [{"arabic": "فهذه علامات المحبة، فمن تمت فيه هذه العلامات فقد تمت محبته وخلص حبه فصفا في الآخرة شرابه وعذب مشربه، ومن امتزج بحبه حب غير الله تنعم في الآخرة بقدر حبه، إذ يمزج شرابه بقدر من شراب المقربين كما قال تعالى في الأبرار: \"إن الأبرار لفي نعيم\" ثم قال: \"يسقون من رحيق مختوم مسك وفي ذلك فليتنافس المتنافسون ومزاجه من تسنيم عيناً يشرب بها المقربون\" فإذا طاب شراب الأبرار لشوب الشراب الصرف الذي هو للمقربين. والشراب عبارة عن جملة نعيم الجنان، كما أن الكتاب عبر به عن جميع الأعمال فقال: \"إن كتاب الأبرار لفي عليي", "english": "These are the signs of love (Mahabbah), so whoever has these signs completed in him, then his love has been completed and his love has been purified, so his drink (Sharab) in the Hereafter becomes pure and his drinking place sweet. And whoever mixes with his love love for other than Allah, he enjoys in the Hereafter according to his love, since his drink is mixed with a measure of the drink of the Close Ones (Muqarrabun) as Allah the Exalted said regarding the Righteous (Al-Abrar): 'Indeed the Righteous (Al-Abrar) are in Bliss (Na'im)' then He said: 'They are given to drink of a sealed pure wine (Rahiq), its seal is musk - and for this let the competitors compete - and its mixture is of Tasnim, a spring from which drink those brought near (Muqarrabun).' So if the drink of the Righteous (Al-Abrar) becomes pleasant due to the mixing of the pure drink which is for the Close Ones (Muqarrabun). And the drink (Sharab) is an expression for the totality of the bliss (Na'im) of Paradise (Jinan), just as the Book (Kitab) expressed by it all the deeds, so He said: 'Indeed the record of the Righteous (Al-Abrar) is in Illiyyun' then He said: 'Witnessed by those brought near (Muqarrabun)' so it was a sign of the cause of their record that it rose to where it is witnessed by the Close Ones (Muqarrabun). And just as the Righteous (Al-Abrar) find increase in their state and their knowledge by their closeness to the Close Ones (Muqarrabun) and their witnessing of them, so will be their state in the Hereafter: 'He did not create you nor resurrect you except as a single soul (Nafs), as We began the first creation, We will repeat it' and as Allah the Exalted said: 'A recompense in proportion' meaning the recompense corresponded to their deeds, so the pure was met with the pure from the drink and the mixed was met with the mixed, and the mixing of every drink is according to what preceded of mixing in his love and his deeds: 'So whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it, and whoever does an atom's weight of evil will see it - and indeed Allah does not change the condition of a people until they change what is in themselves - Indeed Allah does not do injustice to the weight of an atom, and if it is a good deed He multiplies it - and if it is the weight of a mustard seed, We will bring it forth, and sufficient are We as accountants.' So whoever his love in the world is his hope for the bliss (Na'im) of Paradise (Jannah) and the Houris (Hur al-'Ayn).", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book6.doc.txt", "book_title": "Love, Longing, Intimacy and Contentment", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Love, Longing, Intimacy and Contentment'", "badge": "Insight"}, {"arabic": "قال أبو حازم اعرض نفسك على كتاب الله تعالى حيث قال إن الأبرار لفي نعيم وان الفجار لفي جحيم قال فأين رحمة الله قال قريب من المحسنين", "english": "Abu Hazim said: Present yourself to the Book of Allah (the Quran) where He said: 'Indeed the Righteous (Al-Abrar) are in Bliss (Na'im)' and 'Indeed the Wicked (Al-Fujjar) are in Blazing Fire (Jahim).' He (Sulayman) said: Then where is the Mercy (Rahmah) of Allah? He said: Close to the Doers of Good (Al-Muhsinin).", "book_file": "vol2_j2-k04.doc.txt", "book_title": "The Lawful and Prohibited", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'The Lawful and Prohibited'", "badge": "Insight"}, {"arabic": "فإن كان قد يسر لك سبيل الخير فأبشر فإنك مبعد عن النار وإن كنت لا تقصد خيرا إلا وتحيط بك العوائق فتدفعه ولا تقصد شرا إلا ويتيسر لك أسبابه فاعلم أنك مقضى عليك فإن دلالة هذا على العاقبة كدلالة المطر على النبات ودلالة الدخان على النار فقد قال الله تعالى: ﴿ إن الأبرار لفى نعيم وإن الفجار لفى جحيم ﴾ {} فاعرض نفسك على الآيتين وقد عرفت مستقرك من الدارين والله أعلم.", "english": "If the path of good has been made easy for you, then rejoice, for you are kept far from the Fire. And if you do not intend good except that obstacles surround you and repel it, and you do not intend evil except that its causes are made easy for you, then know that you are decreed against. For the indication of this upon the outcome is like the indication of rain upon vegetation and the indication of smoke upon fire. Indeed, Allah the Exalted has said: 'Indeed, the Righteous (Al-Abrar) are in Bliss (Na'eem), and indeed, the Wicked (Al-Fujjar) are in Blazing Fire (Jahim).' So present yourself upon the two verses, and you have known your abode from the two abodes. And Allah knows best.", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book10.doc.txt", "book_title": "Book of Repentance", "content_type": "afterlife", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on death, the grave, and preparation for the Hereafter, from 'Book of Repentance'", "badge": "Afterlife"}, {"arabic": "خلق الجنة وخلق لها أهلا فاستعملهم بالطاعة وخلق النار وخلق لها أهلا فاستعمله بالمعاصي وعرف الخلق علامة أهل الجنة وأهل النار فقال إن الأبرار لفي نعيم وإن الفجار لفي جحيم ثم قال تعالى فيما روى عن نبيه صلى الله عليه وسلم هؤلاء في الجنة ولا أبالي وهؤلاء في النار ولا أبالي", "english": "He created Paradise and created for it people, so He employed them with obedience, and He created Hell and created for it people, so He employed them with disobedience. And He made known to the creation the sign of the people of Paradise and the people of Hell, so He said: 'Indeed, the righteous (Al-Abrar) are in bliss (Na'im), and indeed, the wicked (Al-Fujjar) are in a Blazing Fire (Jahim).' Then He, the Exalted, said in what is narrated from His Prophet (peace be upon him): 'These are in Paradise, and I do not care, and these are in Hell, and I do not care.'", "book_file": "vol3_j3-k01.doc.txt", "book_title": "Disciplining the Soul", "content_type": "afterlife", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on death, the grave, and preparation for the Hereafter, from 'Disciplining the Soul'", "badge": "Afterlife"}], "19": [{"arabic": "يوم لا تجزى نفس عن نفس شيئا ويوم تشخص فيه الأبصار ويوم لا يغنى مولى عن مولى شيئا ويوم لا تملك نفس لنفس شيئا ويوم يدعون إلى نار جهنم دعا ويوم يسحبون فى النار على وجوههم ويوم تقلب وجوههم فى النار ويوم لا يجزى والد عن ولده ويوم يفر المرء من أخيه وأمه وأبيه ويوم لا ينطقون ولا يؤذن لهم فيعتذرون يوم لا مرد له من الله يوم هم بارزون ويوم هم على النار يفتنون يوم لا ينفع مال ولا بنون يوم لا ينفع الظالمين معذرتهم ولهم اللعنة ولهم سوء الدار يوم ترد فيه المعاذير وتبلى السرائر وتظهر الضمائر وتكشف الأستار يوم ", "english": "A day when no soul (Nafs) will be recompensed for another soul (Nafs) anything, and a day when the eyes will stare, and a day when a protector (Mawlā) will not avail a protector (Mawlā) anything, and a day when no soul (Nafs) will possess for another soul (Nafs) anything, and a day when they will be called to the fire of Hell with a call, and a day when they will be dragged in the Fire on their faces, and a day when their faces will be turned over in the Fire, and a day when a parent will not be recompensed for his child, and a day when a man will flee from his brother and his mother and his father, and a day when they will not speak nor will they be permitted so they may apologize, a day when there is no repelling it from Allah, a day when they are exposed, and a day when they are over the Fire being tested, a day when wealth will not benefit nor children, a day when the excuses of the wrongdoers will not benefit them, and for them is the curse and for them is the evil abode, a day when the excuses will be returned and the secrets will be tested and the consciences will appear and the veils will be uncovered, a day when the eyes will be humbled and the voices will be stilled and the turning will be little in it and the hidden things will be exposed and the sins will appear, a day when the servants will be driven and with them the witnesses, and the young will turn gray and the old will be intoxicated, so on that day the scales will be set up and the records will be spread out and Hell will be made manifest and the boiling water will be heated and the Fire will roar and the disbelievers will despair and the fires will be kindled and the colors will change and the tongue will be silenced and the limbs of the human being will speak, so O human being, what has deluded you concerning your Lord (Rabb) the Generous, when the doors were closed and the curtains were lowered and you concealed yourself from the creatures so you committed immorality, so what will you do when your limbs have testified against you? So woe, all woe to us, the company of the heedless ones. Allah sends to us the master of the messengers and sends down upon him the clear Book and informs us with these attributes from the descriptions of the Day of Recompense (Yawm al-Dīn), then He makes us recognize our heedlessness and says: \"Say...\"", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book10.doc.txt", "book_title": "Book of Repentance", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Book of Repentance'", "badge": "Insight"}]}, "wordTiming": {"abdulbasit": {"1": [[1, 350, 1324], [2, 1324, 3618], [3, 3618, 5017]], "2": [[1, 350, 1618], [2, 1618, 3356], [3, 3356, 4625]], "3": [[1, 250, 1370], [2, 1370, 2615], [3, 2615, 3600]], "4": [[1, 250, 1325], [2, 1325, 2519], [3, 2519, 3574]], "5": [[1, 350, 1387], [2, 1387, 2152], [3, 2152, 3152], [4, 3152, 4374], [5, 4374, 6010]], "6": [[1, 400, 2802], [2, 2802, 4272], [3, 4272, 4883], [4, 4883, 5787], [5, 5787, 6903], [6, 6903, 8265]], "7": [[1, 350, 1439], [2, 1439, 2446], [3, 2446, 4349], [4, 4349, 5566]], "8": [[1, 400, 1631], [2, 1631, 2592], [3, 2592, 3748], [4, 3748, 4766], [5, 4766, 6314], [6, 6314, 7508]], "9": [[1, 350, 1304], [2, 1304, 1743], [3, 1743, 3372], [4, 3372, 4808]], "10": [[1, 350, 1626], [2, 1626, 3039], [3, 3039, 4913]], "11": [[1, 250, 1873], [2, 1873, 3469]], "12": [[1, 350, 1908], [2, 1908, 2471], [3, 2471, 3920]], "13": [[1, 350, 1197], [2, 1197, 2904], [3, 2904, 3